## Included content<a id="content"></a>

|     Module     | What it does |
| -------------- | ------------ |
| `fixture`      | Changes the settings of one existing object |
| `fixture_info` | Reads one object without changing it |
| `fixture_plan` | Reports what `fixture` would change, without changing it |

Each module documents its options, return values and own rules:

```sh
ansible-doc {{ namespace }}.{{ collection_name }}.fixture
```


## Requirements<a id="requirements"></a>

You prepare the following on each managed host before the first task:

- The product, installed and set up.
- The credential the product asks for, stored in Ansible Vault or another
  secret store.
- Python 3.9 or newer, GNU `timeout` and `/usr/bin/env`.
- The user the product's command runs as. The modules do not switch users; the
  play uses `become` for that.
- FIXME The fixture also needs a seeded private directory. Replace this item
  with what the product needs.

The control node needs ansible-core
{{ min_ansible_version | default('2.19.0') }} or newer.

